 "procedure": [
  "pairs: every ordered pair (base, claim) of two different claims with the claim core (core is true); sorted by the number in the base's id, then in the claim's",
  "unit claim: at least unit_min_links linked passages, and at least unit_share of them from one unit",
  "level: the base is a unit claim, the claim is not, and their constructs share a string",
  "shared passages: at least shared_min passages linked to both, counting only passages linked to at most shared_cap claims",
  "chaining: the base's outcome is not empty and not 'none', and its content words and the content words of the claim's constructs joined by spaces share at least chain_min; content words: the runs of a-z in the lower-cased text, 3 letters or more, not in stop",
  "stated tie: a passage linked to both whose stub, a space and its gloss (if any), lower-cased, contain a phrase",
  "draw: one random.Random(seed); for bechky then pratt, rng.sample(others, sample[paper]), others being the sorted pairs that are not candidates; then, for bechky then pratt, rng.shuffle of the paper's candidates and sample together, sorted as the pairs are; numbered P001 onward in the shuffled order",
  "table applies when the unit claims with an outcome come from at least two units; its units are those units, in the order of their claims, each with its first such claim; contrasts apply when the index has contrast pairs; factors when either applies"
 ],
